  "_about": "Itinerary demo: the same Mallorca trip (Villa Sóller, 7 nights) and nine friends as the other demos, with Leo (u5) signed in. The trip is UPCOMING, so every date is relative to the day of recording ({today+2} = two days after it; capture/record_video.py resolves them on load). The feed orders a day by sortIndex (the group's drag order), not by time, and day 1 is deliberately out of order: dinner at 20:30 is filed before the 11:00 beach and the 16:00 check-in. Dragging the dinner to the end of day 1 makes the day chronological (a PATCH /activities/reorder). Day 2 holds only the 10:00 boat day, because a new activity lands LAST in its day (the app sends no sortIndex, and the mock appends): the itinerary_demo scenario's 14:00 Beach Club then follows it in order. Every write goes to an in-memory copy, never to this file.",
